  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 105 PM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nWidespread rainfall overnight and this morning produced between\na half inch near I-64 to hot spots over 3 inches in the southern\nhalf of the area today. Pockets of heavier rain is continuing\nacross southwest Kentucky with lingering light rain behind it.\nThe surface front runs from the Missouri Bootheel to about\nMadisonville, KY at 1pm and will continue as low march south.\nOverrunning ascent above the cold front is redeveloping clouds\nand light rain over southeast Missouri and that redevelopment\ncould continue for another couple of hours. Subtle ascent above\nthe frontal zone will likely keep some cloud cover in place\nacross the southern half of the area, with a small chance of a\nshower or two as well through the day Saturday. Although there\nshould be a sharp cutoff between grungy low clouds and generally\nclear skies.\n\nAnother little shot of drier and slightly cooler air arrives\nMonday before a surface ridge axis passes to the east of the\narea and shifts our flow a little more southerly. The trend for\ntemperatures in the mid to late week next week is upward and the\nprobability of highs going back above 80 degrees is above 50%\nand climbing. Overall conditions look dry through this period.",
